      "assert": {
        "claim": "v2579 A flag that lies is worse than no flag",
        "expr": "window.__swekMesher && window.__swekMesher.requested === 'greedy' && window.__swekMesher.used === 'greedy'",
        "why": "?mesher=greedy must actually RUN the greedy mesher; a silent fallback renders the old mesh while reporting the new one"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "face-mirror",
      "url": "/face-mirror.html",
      "wait": 6000,
      "note": "v3110 -- MediaPipe FaceLandmarker via a FAKE camera (--use-fake-device-for-media-stream). The pixel checks answer 'did it render'; the probe answers 'did it stay responsive', which no pixel check can see. detectForVideo() is synchronous and is called from a rAF tick with no worker, so this page is where that costs something. Tracking a REAL face is still a human check at the rig.",
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "notAllBlack",
          "minNonBlackFrac": 0.02
        },
        {
          "type": "notUniform",
          "minUniqueColors": 8
        }
      ],
      "probe": "@mainThreadResponsiveness"
    },
    {
      "name": "population",
      "url": "/population.html",
      "canvas": "grid",
      "wait": 2500,
      "noConsoleErrors": true,
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "notAllBlack",
          "minNonBlackFrac": 0.05
        },
        {
          "type": "notUniform",
          "minUniqueColors": 2
        }
      ],
      "note": "v3120 -- the planner grid is the pixel check; the GPU compile is exercised by the button and surfaces as a pageerror if a shader fails to compile. UNSUPPORTED is reported in the page and is NOT an error."
    },
    {
      "name": "economy",
      "url": "/economy.html",
      "canvas": null,
      "wait": 1500,
      "noConsoleErrors": true,
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "notAllBlack",
          "minNonBlackFrac": 0.02
        }
      ],
      "note": "v3135 -- the page was linked from server.html and render-qa never opened it. It renders WITHOUT spaceprojectsim running (every handler checks d.ok and shows the named failure), so a sim-less QA box is a valid pass here rather than a skip."
    },
    {
      "name": "sphere-impostor",
      "url": "/sphere-impostor.html",
      "canvas": "#sphere",
      "wait": 900,
      "noConsoleErrors": true,
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "notAllBlack",
          "minNonBlackFrac": 0.05
        },
        {
          "type": "terminatorBow",
          "minBow": 0.05
        }
      ],
      "note": "v3180 -- THE SPHERE PANEL MUST BOW. terminatorBow walks the region row by row and reports the SPREAD of the light/dark crossings as a fraction of width; a sphere's terminator curves, so the spread is large. Synthetic validation: a straight boundary measures 0.0000 and a bowed one 0.2833. A box with no WebGL2 shows a NAMED unsupported banner rather than a blank canvas, so a capability-less QA machine is a valid pass and not evidence the page works (v3135's reasoning, RESTORED after v3180's rewrite dropped it)."
    },
    {
      "name": "sphere-impostor-flat",
      "url": "/sphere-impostor.html",
      "canvas": "#flat",
      "wait": 900,
      "noConsoleErrors": true,
      "checks": [
        {
          "type": "notAllBlack",
          "minNonBlackFrac": 0.05
        },
        {
          "type": "terminatorBow",
          "maxBow": 0.03
        }
      ],
      "note": "v3180 -- THE FLAT PANEL MUST NOT BOW, and this half is what makes the other half mean anything. A check that only demanded 'the sphere bows' would pass on a page that drew TWO spheres. THE FAILING CASE HAS TO BE MEASURED FAILING. Both entries load the same URL and screenshot different canvases."
    },
    {
      "name": "raymarch-live",
      "url": "/raymarch-live.html",
      "canvas": "#c",
      "wait": 1200,
      "noConsoleErrors": true,
      "checks": [
